WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.135
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show,"
ladies and gentlemen!

00:00:03.135 --> 00:00:05.972
Thank you for being here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:07.473
I am pumped about this.

00:00:07.473 --> 00:00:11.310
From the new movie "F9,"
Vin Diesel is here tonight!

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:13.747
[ Cheers and applause ]
In studio!

00:00:15.781 --> 00:00:18.384
That's right. I can't wait to
interview one of the few people

00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:20.520
who actually worked out
during the pandemic.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.121
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.121 --> 00:00:23.823
And just a heads-up --
Vin's running a little late,

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:25.759
so don't be alarmed
if a Dodge Charger

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:27.960
comes crashing through the wall.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.630
That's right.
Vin's here to talk about "F9."

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:33.633
And the rumor is that in
this movie they go to space.

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:35.535
[ Audience oohs ]

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:38.070
Not to be confused with Vin's
other space movie coming out

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:40.473
where he plays sexy Jeff Bezos.

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:42.308
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:46.513
Let's get to some news.

00:00:46.513 --> 00:00:48.848
It just came out
that Trump's former bodyguard

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:51.584
is the latest member
of the Trump Organization

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:54.420
to be investigated
by New York prosecutors.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.422
And get this.
The guy's name is --

00:00:56.422 --> 00:00:57.823
And I'm not making this up.

00:00:57.823 --> 00:01:00.326
The guy's name
is Matthew Calamari.

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:02.262
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:08.534
Can we take a look
at Matthew Calamari?

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:10.836
-Yep.
-Yeah.

00:01:10.836 --> 00:01:13.005
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:13.005 --> 00:01:15.842
-Come on. His name
had to be Matthew Calamari.

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:18.044
Looks like a bouncer
at Olive Garden.

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:20.613
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:22.381
No word yet on Trump's
other bodyguards,

00:01:22.381 --> 00:01:24.684
Johnny Meatballs,
Vinnie Calzone,

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:27.086
and Sammy Shrimp Scampi.

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:29.456
-Hey! Oh!

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:31.858
-Sammy Shrimp Scampi.
That's very good.

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:33.759
Well, guys, the White House says

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:36.162
that the country will need
a few extra weeks to hit

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:41.133
President Biden's goal
of 70% vaccination by July 4th.

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:43.169
That's right. The White House
wants to hit its goal so badly,

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.971
instead of fireworks,
they're just going to shoot

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:47.206
a bunch of Pfizer needles
into the sky.

00:01:47.206 --> 00:01:49.509
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:52.645
"Thank you!

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:55.148
That was beautiful.
That's the finale.

00:01:56.815 --> 00:01:59.218
I think that's the finale now."

00:01:59.218 --> 00:02:00.687
"No, no, no. Just wait."

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:02.755
"No, no, I know. That's it.

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:05.958
Wait, wait, wait.
That's the final--

00:02:05.958 --> 00:02:07.527
It was Matthew Calamari."

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:09.161
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:09.161 --> 00:02:14.066
According to projections, it
will be around 68% by July 4th.

00:02:14.066 --> 00:02:16.169
Don't worry, though. Today --

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:18.404
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:21.774
Today, Biden changed
the name of his plan

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.476
to Operation Close Enough.

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:25.445
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:27.480
Well, some TV news --
last night was yet another

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.515
emotional episode
of "The Bachelorette."

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:31.250
We love that show,
and one of the --

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:32.785
[ Applause ]
I know. It's good.

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:34.620
One of the most memorable
moments

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:37.690
was when Hunter and Thomas
got into a heated argument

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:42.295
about whether Thomas was on
the show for the right reason.

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:43.629
If you missed it, don't worry,

00:02:43.629 --> 00:02:45.364
because here
to re-enact that scene

00:02:45.364 --> 00:02:47.833
with actual lines from the show

00:02:47.833 --> 00:02:50.803
are The Roots' own
Tariq and Questlove.

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:52.505
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.941
♪♪

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:57.009
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:57.009 --> 00:02:58.510
-Thanks, Jimmy.

00:02:58.510 --> 00:02:59.812
Tonight I'll be playing Hunter,

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:03.482
a 34-year-old single father
from Texas

00:03:03.482 --> 00:03:07.020
who's concerned that Thomas
is only here for fame,

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:11.291
not to find love, like I am.

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:13.025
-And I'll be playing Thomas,

00:03:13.025 --> 00:03:15.495
a 28-year-old real-estate
broker from California

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:19.165
who doesn't feel like
he's doing anything wrong.

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:21.934
-Very good, guys.
Whenever you're ready.

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:25.971
[ Dramatic music plays ]

00:03:25.971 --> 00:03:28.874
-So, I hear the conversations
that are taking place

00:03:28.874 --> 00:03:30.443
with you and other people,

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:34.113
and there's this flipping and
flopping and constant smiles.

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:38.051
I mean, it feels --
it feels almost like a campaign.

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:40.452
You know?
Like you want to be Bachelor.

00:03:40.452 --> 00:03:42.722
I mean, is that something
you thought about?

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:45.258
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:47.760
-I would never do anything
to hurt you,

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:52.465
so to feel that I come
across in any way that is --

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:54.533
This is the result --
-See?

00:03:54.533 --> 00:03:58.871
See? That's the problem.
The -- I feel manipulated.

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:01.040
It just makes me really worried
about Katie

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.609
because you could be
doing the same thing with her.

00:04:03.609 --> 00:04:07.413
And I would like to know --
have you ever thought

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:10.116
maybe I could end up
being the Bachelor?

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:12.952
♪♪

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:16.488
-I want to say
I appreciate you for being so --

00:04:16.488 --> 00:04:19.892
-Has being the Bachelor...

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:22.328
crossed your mind?

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:24.363
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.363 --> 00:04:26.899
-I...don't have
the right answer bec--

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:29.202
-So is that your answer? Yes?

00:04:29.202 --> 00:04:31.504
You are thinking about
being the Bachelor.

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:33.873
Is that what you were saying?

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:35.908
-Uh, look,
bef-- before coming here,

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:37.677
I didn't know what to expect.

00:04:37.677 --> 00:04:43.482
-I'm not asking
what you expected-uh!

00:04:43.482 --> 00:04:46.319
Was being the Bachelor...

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:50.289
Was that a prerogative for you?

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:54.027
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:55.461
-Okay.

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:57.663
I can be just genuine
to you guys,

00:04:57.663 --> 00:04:59.766
and I'm not gonna be.

00:04:59.766 --> 00:05:02.735
So...yes.

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:05.871
Coming into this -- this --
I had thoughts in my mind

00:05:05.871 --> 00:05:07.874
that I was potentially
gonna be the --

00:05:07.874 --> 00:05:09.475
the next Bachelor.

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:12.211
-Like, that's messed up.

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:14.780
♪♪

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:18.450
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:21.787
-Touching. Thanks, guys.
Questlove and Tariq, everyone.

00:05:21.787 --> 00:05:23.455
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:23.455 --> 00:05:26.425
Thank you. Gosh.
Whew. That was emotional.

00:05:26.425 --> 00:05:28.161
Wow.

00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:30.462
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.462 --> 00:05:34.167
Some business news. Coors
just launched a new ice cream

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:36.301
that is infused
with their hard seltzer.

00:05:36.301 --> 00:05:39.138
Yep. They didn't pitch that
on "Shark Tank."

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:41.107
They pitched that
on "Drunk Tank."

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:43.009
-Oh.
-You'll know it's good when

00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:45.311
the ice-cream truck
accidentally pulls up

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:46.578
in your front lawn.

00:05:46.578 --> 00:05:48.714
[ Steve imitates
tires screeching ]

00:05:48.714 --> 00:05:52.785
And, finally, I saw that NASA
sent dozens of baby squid

00:05:52.785 --> 00:05:56.922
from Hawaii to the International
Space Station for research.

00:05:56.922 --> 00:05:58.624
-Ooh.
-And I also heard that

00:05:58.624 --> 00:06:01.861
the mission is being led
by commander Matthew Calamari.

